(Stage 1d — a mixed element passed to a function taking `a value`
 retains its runtime tag, so the stage-1c predicates inside the callee
 classify each element correctly. The function is void and prints inside,
 so this isolates value-parameter tag propagation from return-type tracking.
 Acceptance criterion 1.)

To describe with a value called item.
  If item is a text, print "a text".
  Otherwise if item is a decimal, print "a decimal".
  Otherwise print "a number".

a list called m is [1, "two", 3.5].
For each item in m,
  describe of item.